le panels cascading down her sides, the bodice wrapped in soft pleated folds, both hands resting loosely by her hips with the gown's translucent skirts billowing gently around her legs, the pale flower petals suspended mid-air drifting around her in the light shaft and a carpet of matching petals scattered across the luminous floor beneath her train. The camera holds a very slow, small-amplitude Push In at near-static speed throughout the full shot, the scene remaining single-camera, no cuts. During the first two seconds, the petals that are frozen in <Picture 1> continue their natural drift: the ones on the left arc downward and to the right in soft spirals while the ones on the right drift gently downward and to the left, their motion perfectly continuous from the still. The translucent tulle layers of the gown's train, slightly lifted at the hem in the reference frame, settle and ripple as if stirred by a soft invisible breeze from the top of the light beam. At roughly three seconds, her left hand, relaxed by her side, begins the most minute turn — the fingers flex gently and the palm rotates fractionally inward toward her thigh, as if she is about to reach out. Her eyelids, already open in the reference, soften their gaze and blink once, very slowly. The top-down light beam pulses imperceptibly brighter for a heartbeat, sending a faint wave of motes and airborne dust through the shaft of illumination. Over the following seconds, more petals begin to descend from out of frame at the top, joining the existing ones, so the drift slowly intensifies without ever becoming hurried; the petals always maintain their soft ivory hue. The pleated tulle covering the shoulders catches the light more strongly as the material shifts slightly with her nearly imperceptible weight transfer onto her right leg. By the final two seconds, her expression has settled from the neutral calm of the opening into the faintest possible upward tilt at the corner of her mouth — a quiet, almost-whispered hint of a smile that never breaks into anything larger. Several of the largest drifting petals pass gently across the front of the light beam very close to the lens, blurring softly in the foreground before drifting out at the sides. The glow of the top-down beam begins a slow, almost imperceptible fade toward warmer tones, the silvery cool light shifting barely noticeably toward soft champagne gold. By the end of the 15 seconds, the Push In has brought the camera to a gently closer medium framing that still preserves the full gown train and the light shaft in view; the petals continue their drift naturally; the gown's tulle ripples gently in the same invisible breeze; the woman's faint near-smile and the warm-tinged top beam settle the image into its final held moment with perfect continuity from the starting reference picture.\n\noverall_soundscape: A pure, breathy high-altitude silence filled only by the faintest sustained air tone, occasionally punctuated by the almost-inaudible soft pap of a single petal grazing another mid-air and the subtle chiffon-like rustle of tulle fabric moving with the invisible breeze. No other environmental sounds enter.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A single held high celesta note at a very slow tempo, joined after a few seconds by a single clear harp arpeggio that rises gently and repeats with minute variations, volume held low and distant, never overpowering the air tone and gradually fading into warm soft reverb by the final moment.", 1344, 768, 73], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 241, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"name": "vae", "link": 242, "label": "vae", "type": "VAE", "localized_name": "vae"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "first_frame", "link": 262, "label": "first_frame", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "first_frame"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "last_frame", "label": "last_frame", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "last_frame"}, {"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "label": "prompt",